===Etymology===
{{etyl|fr|en}}, believed to be named after the village of Chardonnay in the [[w:Mâconnais|Mâconnais]] region of France, where [[w:Pouilly-Fuissé|Pouilly-Fuissé]] is currently produced; it is possible that the variety was first bred there

The place name Chardonnay is from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|Cardonnacum}}.

[[Category:English terms derived from toponyms]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[green]]-[[skin]]ned [[grape]] [[variety]] used to make a [[white wine]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A variety of wine made from this grape.

